{
	"_comment": "THE loader manifest — the single source of truth for the engine's file list, load order, and the canonical data-file map. Consumers: reference/tests/_engine_load.cjs (used by the node harnesses: batch_convert.cjs and all _verify_*.cjs) and reference/tests/_check_index_sync.cjs (which checks app/index.html's <script> tags against this list, and this list against the actual app/js/*.js files on disk). Adding or splitting an engine file means editing THIS file AND index.html — the sync check fails loudly if they ever drift. This replaces the old hand-maintained require() list, whose fragility used to silently break the widget verifiers.",
	"_node_note": "node_order is the exact order the node batch converter needs (Utils first; TemplateModeResolver after ContentConverter). Files that appear in browser_order but NOT in node_order are browser-only: Config (UI), DataService (the node harnesses build their own with a custom FetchOembed), ZipWriter, SummaryReporter, App.",
